Are you waking up sweaty or restless at 2 a.m.?

Are you lying in bed for 40 minutes before you finally fall asleep?

Are you sick of a blaring alarm clock jolting you into a groggy morning?

All of those point to one core issue: temperature regulation.

And according to my podcast guest, @Dr_MichaelBreus, correcting that single pattern can dramatically improve your entire night of sleep. In this episode, we break down the physiology behind thermal sleep architecture—and the technology that now allows you to control it with precision.��We cover:��❄️ The role of core body temperature in signaling the brain to initiate sleep�🛏️ The strengths and limitations of today’s mattress cooling systems�🔥 The impact of strategic warming–cooling cycles on sleep depth, including warm feet, pre-bed heat exposure, and why night sweats happen�✈️ Michael’s travel sleep playbook, including airplane seating, hotel room setup, and the gear he brings with him��Comment “SLEEP” for the link, or listen ad-free on @JoinLIFENetwork.

